---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can I click through safely?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "For a certificate you just issued and understand: maybe. For any public site: never, because that is exactly what phishing relies on."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Why does it work in one browser and not another?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Different certificate stores and HSTS state. Test in a private window and a second browser."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is an intermediate certificate?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The CA’s signing certificate linking yours to the trusted root; servers must serve it along with the leaf."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does Let's Encrypt expire faster?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Yes: 90 days versus a year, by design for automation. Missing a renewal fails the same way any expiry does."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "My site works but shows not secure in the address bar",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "That is mixed content, not a certificate error: an HTTPS page loading HTTP subresources."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="SSL Certificate Errors: Causes and Fixes | PromptDNS"
  description="Every SSL certificate error explained: NET::ERR_CERT_DATE_INVALID, authority errors, name mismatches, and the fix for each by cause."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ssl-tls/" class="hover:text-accent">SSL/TLS Guides</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Certificate Errors</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">SSL Certificate Errors: Causes and Fixes</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Certificate errors block pages outright with distinct error names. Each name is a diagnosis: expired, wrong name, untrusted chain, or self-signed. Match the error to the cause below and the fix is usually mechanical.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The error decoder</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60"><table class="pdns-table"><thead><tr><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">NET::ERR_CERT_DATE_INVALID</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Expired (or not yet valid) certificate</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Renew now; check server clock for not-yet-valid</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">NET::ERR_CERT_COMMON_NAME_INVALID</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Certificate does not cover this hostname</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Add the name to the SANs or issue a matching certificate</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">NET::ERR_CERT_AUTHORITY_INVALID</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Chain not trusted: self-signed or missing intermediate</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Install the full chain; replace self-signed with a CA certificate</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">ERR_SSL_VERSION_OR_CIPHER_MISMATCH</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">No common TLS version/cipher</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Enable TLS 1.2/1.3 with modern suites</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">NET::ERR_CERT_REVOKED</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Certificate revoked by its CA</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Reissue immediately; investigate why it was revoked</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">HSTS errors</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Policy forces HTTPS and something is broken</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Fix the underlying TLS problem; HSTS blocks overrides</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The universal diagnosis flow</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Click the warning, view the certificate: check dates, then Subject Alternative Names, then the issuer chain.</li><li>Test with an external checker (SSL Labs) to see the chain as strangers see it: missing intermediates often work on your machine via cached chains.</li><li>Confirm the certificate is served for THIS hostname: shared infrastructure sometimes serves the wrong vhost’s certificate.</li></ol>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Prevention</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Automated renewal (ACME/Let’s Encrypt) or managed certificates on your platform.</li><li>Expiry monitoring with alerts at 30 days.</li><li>Deploy the full chain (leaf + intermediates), and include every hostname variant in SANs.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I click through safely?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">For a certificate you just issued and understand: maybe. For any public site: never, because that is exactly what phishing relies on.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Why does it work in one browser and not another?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Different certificate stores and HSTS state. Test in a private window and a second browser.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is an intermediate certificate?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The CA’s signing certificate linking yours to the trusted root; servers must serve it along with the leaf.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does Let's Encrypt expire faster?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Yes: 90 days versus a year, by design for automation. Missing a renewal fails the same way any expiry does.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">My site works but shows not secure in the address bar<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">That is mixed content, not a certificate error: an HTTPS page loading HTTP subresources.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/mixed-content-fix/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Mixed content fixes →</a></li><li><a href="/tls-versions-explained/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">TLS versions →</a></li><li><a href="/certificate-authorities-explained/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Certificate authorities →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
